---
// Ported from the Claude Design canvas artboard CaseTreeService.dc.html. Edit the canvas, then re-port.
import BaseV2 from '../../layouts/BaseV2.astro';
---
<BaseV2 title="The Tree Service · Paramore.Design" description="A field-ops tool that replaced four SaaS subscriptions, designed and built solo in four weeks.">
  <!-- BLOCK: Case hero -->
  <section class="pd-wrap" data-screen-label="Hero">
    <div class="pd-topline">
      <a href="/work" style="text-decoration: none">← All projects</a>
      <span style="color: var(--color-accent-ink)">Client Project // Trades · Operations · AI</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="pd-title" style="margin-top: 40px">The Tree Service</h1>
    <p class="pd-lede" style="margin: 28px 0 40px">A field-ops tool for a tree service company. Replaced four SaaS subscriptions with one tool, designed and built solo in four weeks.</p>
    <!-- BLOCK: Meta strip -->
    <div class="pd-meta">
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Role</span><span class="pd-meta__value">Solo Designer-Developer</span></div>
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Timeline</span><span class="pd-meta__value">4 Weeks · 2026</span></div>
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Stack</span><span class="pd-meta__value">Next.js · Supabase · Vercel · Tailwind</span></div>
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">AI</span><span class="pd-meta__value">Claude Code as dev partner</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: TL;DR -->
  <section class="pd-wrap" style="margin-top: 40px" data-screen-label="TL;DR">
    <div class="pd-tldr">
      <div><span class="pd-tldr__label">Context</span><p class="pd-tldr__text">A tree service crew running on paper JSAs, four tools, and a Tupperware of fuel receipts. Admin took an hour every night to reconcile the day.</p></div>
      <div><span class="pd-tldr__label">My role</span><p class="pd-tldr__text">Solo designer-developer: research, design, and the build on Next.js and Supabase, with Claude Code as dev partner.</p></div>
      <div><span class="pd-tldr__label">Outcome</span><p class="pd-tldr__text">One tool retired four subscriptions and seven paper forms. The crew was using it daily four weeks after kickoff.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Hero image + caption -->
  <section class="pd-wrap" style="margin-top: 48px" data-screen-label="Hero image">
    <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/images/projects/TreeServiceHero.webp" alt="The Tree Service daily crew tools and admin dashboard" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9"></div>
    <p class="pd-lede" style="margin-top: 28px; max-width: 70ch">Most field-ops software is built for the office. Brandon’s crew fills it out covered in mulch with chainsaw chaps still on. The brief was simple: rebuild the daily routine from the truck seat backwards, then give the office whatever falls out of that. This is what fell out.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Role & boundaries -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Role and boundaries">
    <div class="pd-head" style="margin-bottom: 24px"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">Role &amp; boundaries</span></div>
    <div class="pd-owners">
      <div>
        <span class="pd-kicker" style="color: var(--color-text)">I owned</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Understanding the crew’s daily routine and the office’s reconciliation work</li>
          <li>Product and interaction design for the crew side and the admin dashboard</li>
          <li>The build: Next.js, Supabase, Vercel, Tailwind</li>
          <li>Data migration: the equipment and driver records</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="pd-kicker" style="color: var(--color-text)">Others owned</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Brandon, the owner: priorities, sign-off, and the form templates he edits himself</li>
          <li>Dayton, the general foreman: [what the field side contributed]</li>
          <li>[Anyone else involved: the accountant, the crew leads]</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="pd-owners__foot">How I worked with them: “Bring me your ideas. Seriously, I am making this for you. How do you want it to work?”</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Numbered list -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Before">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Before</div><h2 class="pd-h2">The stack Brandon <span class="pd-accent">already had.</span></h2>
        <p class="pd-body" style="margin-top: 20px">The crew wasn’t the problem. The tools were too generic, and admin took an hour every night reconciling four sources to know what happened that day.</p></div>
      <ul class="pd-list">
        <li><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">Paper JSAs.</strong> Filled out at the yard, then forgotten on the dashboard. No record of who signed what.</li>
        <li><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">Versabit.</strong> $50/mo. Abandoned because nobody could onboard a crew member without a half-day of training.</li>
        <li><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">Samsara.</strong> $35/mo per truck. Gives location. Gives nothing else.</li>
        <li><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">Tupperware.</strong> A literal Tupperware on the office shelf, full of fuel receipts. The accountant’s least favorite drawer.</li>
        <li><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">A spreadsheet.</strong> One list of equipment. Half of it accurate. The other half in someone’s head.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Statement -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Approach">
    <div class="pd-quote">
      <p class="pd-quote__text">One tool, four subscriptions <span class="pd-accent">retired.</span></p>
      <p class="pd-body" style="margin-top: 20px">I designed for the truck instead of the office, and shipped a single tool that replaced the whole stack. Every decision had to survive the same test: does this make a guy in gloves faster, or slower?</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Split (image left) -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Designed for the truck">
    <div class="pd-split">
      <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/images/projects/TreeServiceIpad.webp" alt="The daily checklist on an iPad" style="aspect-ratio: 626 / 551"></div>
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Daily checklist</div><h2 class="pd-h2">Designed for the truck.</h2><p class="pd-body" style="margin-top: 20px">Filled out each morning before the crew leaves the yard. 90 seconds, signed digitally, done.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Split (flipped) -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Worksite details">
    <div class="pd-split pd-split--flip">
      <div class="pd-frame" style="max-width: 360px; justify-self: center"><img src="/assets/images/projects/in-flight.webp" alt="A pre-trip vehicle inspection in progress on a phone, with pass and fail buttons"></div>
      <div>
        <div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Worksite details</div>
        <h2 class="pd-h2">What makes it <span class="pd-accent">not suck</span> on a worksite.</h2>
        <p class="pd-body" style="margin-top: 20px">The crew uses this in gloves. Half of them have rural cell service. None of them want a forgotten password between them and a paying job.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Key decisions -->
  <section class="pd-wrap" style="margin-top: 48px" data-screen-label="Decisions">
    <div class="pd-head" style="margin-bottom: 0"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">Key decisions</span><span class="pd-kicker">Each one had to make a guy in gloves faster</span></div>
    <div class="pd-decisions" style="border-top: 0">
      <div class="pd-decision">
        <h3 class="pd-decision__title">Tap your name, enter a PIN</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Options</dt><dd>Usernames, email and passwords; or tap your name and enter a short PIN.</dd>
          <dt>Why</dt><dd>No usernames, no email, no “forgot password” at the yard.</dd>
          <dt class="is-tradeoff">Trade-off</dt><dd class="is-tradeoff">[Less security than full accounts on a shared device; say how you scoped that risk.]</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-decision">
        <h3 class="pd-decision__title">48px touch targets</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Options</dt><dd>A standard, denser web UI; or targets sized for gloved hands.</dd>
          <dt>Why</dt><dd>Gloves don’t do thumbnail-sized buttons.</dd>
          <dt class="is-tradeoff">Trade-off</dt><dd class="is-tradeoff">[Less on each screen; where that forced extra steps.]</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-decision">
        <h3 class="pd-decision__title">Camera-first capture</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Options</dt><dd>Typed entry and file uploads; or open straight to the camera.</dd>
          <dt>Why</dt><dd>Receipts, defect photos, and signatures land directly in storage. No copy-paste, no data URLs. AI parses the receipts.</dd>
          <dt class="is-tradeoff">Trade-off</dt><dd class="is-tradeoff">[What happens with a bad photo or no signal, and how you handled it.]</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-decision">
        <h3 class="pd-decision__title">Version-locked submissions</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Options</dt><dd>Render old forms with the current template; or lock each submission to the template version it was signed on.</dd>
          <dt>Why</dt><dd>When Brandon edits a form template, last week’s signed forms still render exactly as the crew filled them. OSHA likes that.</dd>
          <dt class="is-tradeoff">Trade-off</dt><dd class="is-tradeoff">[Storing every template version adds complexity; was it worth it?]</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Full image + caption -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Fleet">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule); margin-bottom: 40px">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Admin</div><h2 class="pd-h2">Manage the <span class="pd-accent">entire fleet.</span></h2></div>
      <p class="pd-body" style="font-size: 17px">43 pieces of equipment imported from Brandon’s insurance schedule on day three. Each one tracks its own maintenance schedule, parts costs, fuel logs, inspection history, and crew assignment.</p>
    </div>
    <figure style="margin: 0">
      <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/images/projects/TreeServiceEquipment.webp" alt="Equipment detail page for a Bobcat E42 with photos, info, crew assignment and maintenance history" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10"></div>
      <figcaption class="pd-figcap"><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">Equipment · Inventory + Detail.</strong> Photos, specs, custom fields, crew assignment, insurance, and a live activity log, per piece, per day.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure style="margin: 48px 0 0">
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Maintenance history · desktop screenshot needed]</div>
      <figcaption class="pd-figcap"><strong style="color: var(--color-text)">Maintenance · History &amp; Spend.</strong> Brandon used to log a parts purchase by writing it on a sticky note. Now he taps Log Work Done, uploads the invoice photo, and the cost rolls up against the equipment’s lifetime spend.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Stats band -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Results">
    <div class="pd-cells">
      <div><div class="pd-stat__value">4 wks</div><div class="pd-stat__label">From kickoff to crew using it daily</div></div>
      <div><div class="pd-stat__value pd-accent">4 → 1</div><div class="pd-stat__label">SaaS subscriptions retired</div></div>
      <div><div class="pd-stat__value">7</div><div class="pd-stat__label">Paper forms eliminated: JSA, pre-trip, aerial-lift, and more</div></div>
      <div><div class="pd-stat__value">43 + 16</div><div class="pd-stat__label">Equipment + drivers migrated to live data on day three</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Quotes -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Quotes">
    <div class="pd-cells pd-cells--wide">
      <figure style="margin: 0"><blockquote class="pd-h3" style="margin: 0; text-transform: none; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2">“I can’t believe how simple this is compared to the <span class="pd-accent">other app we’ve tried before.</span>”</blockquote><figcaption class="pd-kicker" style="margin-top: auto">Dayton, General Foreman</figcaption></figure>
      <figure style="margin: 0"><blockquote class="pd-h3" style="margin: 0; text-transform: none; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2">“This is some seriously awesome sh!t.”</blockquote><figcaption class="pd-kicker" style="margin-top: auto">Brandon, Owner of The Tree Service</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Looking back -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Looking back">
    <div class="pd-lookback">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 12px">Looking back</div><h2 class="pd-h3" style="color: var(--color-bg)">What I’d do differently</h2></div>
      <p>[One honest answer: something you’d design or build differently after watching the crew use it.]</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Closing CTA -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section pd-section--last" data-screen-label="Closing">
    <div class="pd-quote">
      <p class="pd-quote__text">Your business has its own <span class="pd-accent">Tupperware of receipts.</span></p>
      <p class="pd-body" style="margin-top: 20px">I build custom AI-assisted tools for small businesses: one tool, custom-fit, that replaces the stack of half-used SaaS subscriptions you’re paying for. If that sounds like you, let’s talk.</p>
      <div class="pd-btns" style="margin-top: 28px">
        <a href="mailto:hparamore@gmail.com" class="pd-btn pd-btn--primary">Email me →</a>
        <a href="/build" class="pd-btn">How I work with businesses</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Next project -->
  <section class="pd-poster" data-screen-label="Next project">
    <div class="pd-poster__inner" style="padding-block: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px)">
      <a href="/projects/tava" class="pd-next">
        <div><div class="pd-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Next project</div><div class="pd-poster__title" style="font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 88px)">Tava Health</div></div>
        <span class="pd-next__box" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseV2>
